0

1

0

1

1

0

3

2

1

0

Sample Output 3
10

Explanation
Here, N = 10
A = [0, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 3, 2, 1, 0]

We can divide the employees into the following teams: [0,1], [0,1], [1,0,3,2], [1,0]

Expert values:

[0,1] → 2
[0,1] → 2
[1,0,3,2] → 4
[1,0] → 2
So, Expert Number = 2 + 2 + 4 + 2 = 10

Please note that there is no other way to divide the employees such that expert number is greater than 10.

This is the maximum possible expert number.

Input Format

The first line contains an integer, N, denoting the number of elements in A.

Each line i of the N subsequent lines (where 0 ≤ i < N) contains an integer describing A[i].

Constraints

1 <= N <= 10^5

1 <= A[i] <= 10^3

Output Format

Integer denoting the maximum expert number

Sample Input 0

3
0
1
2
Sample Output 0

3
Explanation 0

Explanation
A = [0,1,2]

Single team: [0,1,2]

MEX = 3

Expert Number = 3

Sample Input 1

3
1
1
1
Sample Output 1

0
Explanation 1

Explanation
A = [1,1,1]

No team contains skill 0.

Each team MEX = 0

Maximum expert number = 0



import java.util.*;

public class Solution {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int[] arr = new int[n];
        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++){
            arr[i] = sc.nextInt();
        }                                 
        int[] dp = new int[n + 1];
        dp[0] = 0;
        for(int i = 1; i <= n; i++){
            dp[i] = 0;
            boolean[] present = new boolean[1005];
            int mex = 0;
            for(int j = i; j >= 1; j--){
                present[arr[j - 1]] = true;
                while(present[mex]){
                    mex++;
                }
                dp[i] = Math.max(dp[i], dp[j - 1] + mex);
            }
        }
        System.out.println(dp[n]);
    }
}
